In article <Dm71TB1w165w@netlink.cts.com>, jdriver@netlink.cts.com (John Driver) writes:
>         My copy of the spoilers lists a mail daemon as being a 
> creature in the game.  However, I have never seen one, and when I 
> try to polymorph into one, the game tells me that it has heard of 
> no such creature.  Well, why is it listed in the spoilers?  I am 
> running the dos compile of 3.0j.


mail daemons show up when your user account recieves email...Since DOS
doesn't offer email, Nethack is usually compiled without the mail features,
so the game won't know what you mean by mail daemon.  It's no big loss,
really, since they aren't very powerfull.  Vampire lord is a better choice
to poly into. 

>  
>         Also, how do you guys keep getting these impossibly low 
> AC's?  Even with a +3 dragon scale mail your armor class isn't 
> going to be at -16 like I've seen people posting as theirs.  What's 
> the secret?

The secret is in covering every square inch of yourself in as much armor as
possible.  This itself can take you down to the -20's at least.  For example,
take my current charater, Amil the priest: (a lucky bastard: he found 2 
(yes, count 'em: two) wands of wishing between levels 1-4)
+3 helm of telepathy
+3 gauntlets of dexterity
+3 cloak of displacement
+3 shield of reflection
+3 speed boots
+3 gray dragon scale mail
+3 Hawaiian shirt
This gives him an AC of about -28, I believe.  He gave every last cent to a 
temple priest (400*his level) and got an AC bonus from that too, so he's at
-31 now.  The really gross AC's you see some people mention (in the -60's or
beyond means that they spent mucho time at the temple donating money,
to get the AC bonus...Probably they get the gold to do this by using one of 
the several gold getting abuses.  Then you become totally unscratchable,
but it takes some fun out of the game...As it is, most monsters can barely
touch Amil at -31...To push it further seems like overkill.

